snp1.11:7.1 starts: And on top of that,
snp1.11:7.2 starts: its hollow head is filled with brains.
snp1.11:7.3 starts: The fool, beset by ignorance,
snp1.11:7.4 starts: thinks it beautiful,
snp2.1:7.1 starts: Those who, devoted, firm-minded,
snp2.1:7.2 starts: apply themselves to Gotama’s message,
snp2.1:7.3 starts: on attaining their goal, plunge into the deathless,
snp2.1:7.4 starts: freely enjoying the liberation they’ve gained.
snp2.1:7.5 starts: This, too, is an exquisite treasure in the
snp2.1:7.6 starts: By this truth may there be well-being.
snp2.1:9.1 starts: Those who have seen clearly the noble truths
snp2.1:9.2 starts: well-taught by the one deeply discerning—
snp2.1:9.3 starts: regardless of what [later] might make them heedless—
snp2.1:9.4 starts: will come to no eighth state of becoming,
snp2.1:9.5 starts: This, too, is an exquisite treasure in the
snp2.1:9.6 starts: By this truth may there be well-being.
snp2.3:4.1 starts: Carrying one’s manly burden,
snp2.3:4.2 starts: the fruits & rewards develop
snp2.3:4.3 starts: the conditions that make for joy,
snp2.3:4.4 starts: the bliss that brings praise.
snp1.11:10.1 starts: Having heard the Awakened One’s words,
snp1.11:10.2 starts: the discerning monk
snp1.11:10.3 starts: comprehends,
snp1.11:10.4 starts: for he sees it
snp1.11:11.1 starts: “As this is, so is that.
snp1.11:11.2 starts: As that, so this.”
snp1.11:11.3 starts: Within & without,
snp1.11:11.4 starts: he should let desire for the body
snp1.11:12.1 starts: With desire & passion faded away,
snp1.11:12.2 starts: the discerning monk arrives here:
snp1.11:12.3 starts: at the deathless,
snp1.11:12.4 starts: the unfallen, undying state
snp1.11:13.1 starts: This two-footed thing is cared for,
snp1.11:13.2 starts: filthy, evil-smelling,
snp1.11:13.3 starts: filled with various carcasses,
snp1.11:13.4 starts: oozing out here & there:
snp1.11:14.1 starts: Whoever would think,
snp1.11:14.2 starts: on the basis of a body like
snp1.11:14.3 starts: to exalt himself or disparage another—
snp1.11:14.4 starts: What is that
snp1.12:11.1 starts: From the best
snp1.12:11.2 starts: he receives alms.
snp1.12:11.3 starts: neither flattering
snp1.12:11.4 starts: The enlightened call him a sage.
snp2.2:3.1 starts: Yet you, kinsman of Brahmā, say,
snp2.2:3.2 starts: ‘Raw stench is not proper for me,’
snp2.2:3.3 starts: while consuming cooked rice
snp2.2:3.4 starts: and the well-prepared fleshes of birds.
snp2.2:3.5 starts: So I ask you, Kassapa, the meaning
